{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1015376-how-would-you-do-a-cicada-3301-parody-in-werewolf","id":1015376,"title":"How would you do a Cicada 3301 parody in Werewolf?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-10T15:06:45-08:00","id":1015376,"title":"How would you do a Cicada 3301 parody in Werewolf?","content":"I am thinking about getting Werewolf and i already came up with an antagonist that is basically a parody of Cicada 3301. How would make the parody work. Also, the reason this post is also in Forsaken is because i meant to post it here but i accidentally posted it there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T15:33:25-08:00","id":1015383,"title":"","content":"Well, Cicada 3301 could be anything, from NSA to CIA to Interpol, so there are a lot of options. I would suggest having the images by designed to be only solvable when copied by hand and infused with Gnosis, to make it a mystery that only a creature with Gnosis can solve. It could be a lure, a treasure map, for Fera, and Kinfolk with Gnosis, to follow into a trap where they will be ambushed by servants of the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T15:42:06-08:00","id":1015387,"title":"","content":"I was kinda thinking that the group who made it is controlled by the Weaver. Would it make since if this group is bankrolled by Shinzui Enterprises like how Incognito is bankrolled by Pentex?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T15:50:11-08:00","id":1015391,"title":"","content":"Its possible. The question is why? Is an agent of the Computer trying to ferret out potential recruits to be turned into Drones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T15:54:44-08:00","id":1015393,"title":"","content":"Finding recruits to be turned into drones sounds like a good idea. Also, the group's puzzles can be deadly, especially if they find out it is a fera trying to solve it. By deadly, i meant that a false clue could led a pack to a house full of booby traps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T17:55:41-08:00","id":1015429,"title":"","content":"I imagine that they would have toys like a M18 Claymore filled with 3.2 mm silver balls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T17:59:21-08:00","id":1015431,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Also, I would think it would either be the Glass Walkers or Corax who discover them. Also, the leader of the group views it as a big game and the world is the game map.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T18:32:28-08:00","id":1015449,"title":"","content":"Weaver Drone recruitment center.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T18:34:22-08:00","id":1015453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1015376-how-would-you-do-a-cicada-3301-parody-in-werewolf?p=1015449#post1015449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weaver Drone recruitment center.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is actually one of the ideas I am seriously considering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T12:24:30-08:00","id":1015772,"title":"","content":"Another question. Besides a claymore filled with silver balls, what kind of traps could harm or maim a werewolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T13:55:35-08:00","id":1015823,"title":"","content":"Well, anything with silver would do it. You could have a net of woven silver fall from the ceiling, silver spikes at the bottom of a pit trap, a poison trap that sprays silver dust into the face of the target so they breathe the silver dust in, bear traps made of silver instead of steel, etc.. The great thing about silver traps is that they would work just as well as the equivalent steel traps against most humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T14:01:08-08:00","id":1015830,"title":"","content":"Well that gives the Cicada like group a jigsaw from Saw like feel. Which i have no problem with. Also their first message ends with the phrase,&quot; Wherever you go, we are watching.&quot; This phrase is true do to the fact that they have agents watching every puzzle to see if someone solves them. Also, how should i do combat with these guys? Because a group of computer nerds won't pose a physical threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T15:19:49-08:00","id":1015865,"title":"","content":"I also think that most werewolves really won't have the patience to solve a bunch of puzzles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T18:58:20-08:00","id":1015934,"title":"","content":"Well, Cicada is probably not a bunch of computer nerds, they are probably intelligence analysts and intelligence agents, so they will have access to a lot of resources and operatives, even if they are not backed by the Weaver or Wyrm. I think that the Garou would delegate the solving of the puzzles to their Kinfolk and just go in a pick up the rewards (or the next clue) after the Kinfolk have done the high level intellectual work. You could have them provide video and audio communications to their Kinfolk relatives (especially if they are Glasswalkers) while the Garou go into each location (with the Kinfolk asking them questions based on the video and audio and giving them advice about what to examine and what to look out for). Of course, a jamming signal right before they get to something really interesting would be quite thematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T19:04:15-08:00","id":1015935,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the group does not tolerate cheaters in their game. Also, I am picturing a scene in a bowling alley where the garou are looking for a clue while being watched by two bowlers who may in fact be agents. Also, I have to think of a reason why they are investigating this group. Perhaps a corax went missing while playing the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T19:19:46-08:00","id":1015940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1015376-how-would-you-do-a-cicada-3301-parody-in-werewolf?p=1015865#post1015865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think that most werewolves really won't have the patience to solve a bunch of puzzles.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like pigeonholing, straight up. All werewolves have rage, but this doesn't make them all impatient or stupid. A Garou's predilection for complex problem solving depends on individual, as well as tribe and pack totem. For example, the Stargazers are known for pondering puzzles, and the Uktena are skilled at unraveling hidden mysteries.<br /> <br /> I think that whatever Cicada 3301 is up to, it is likely complex. Very complex. Weaver things are insane, but their Mistress is still viciously subtle. Perhaps this group may be seeking likely individuals who all need to be 'clarified' and the Cicadas are the ones tasked with finding and entrapping them in the Weaver's webs. A Saw-style deathtrap might only be the first step into a larger world of purposeful, clever madness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T19:49:06-08:00","id":1015948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1015376-how-would-you-do-a-cicada-3301-parody-in-werewolf?p=1015940#post1015940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems like pigeonholing, straight up. All werewolves have rage, but this doesn't make them all impatient or stupid. A Garou's predilection for complex problem solving depends on individual, as well as tribe and pack totem. For example, the Stargazers are known for pondering puzzles, and the Uktena are skilled at unraveling hidden mysteries.<br /> <br /> I think that whatever Cicada 3301 is up to, it is likely complex. Very complex. Weaver things are insane, but their Mistress is still viciously subtle. Perhaps this group may be seeking likely individuals who all need to be 'clarified' and the Cicadas are the ones tasked with finding and entrapping them in the Weaver's webs. A Saw-style deathtrap might only be the first step into a larger world of purposeful, clever madness.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bGood point. Also, the owner of this group views this all as a very complex game. Just picture Jigsaw, except with less death traps. Also, the death traps are really for &quot;cheaters&quot;. Also, the organization could be named after a chess piece, but which piece?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 12-11-2016, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T20:06:00-08:00","id":1015952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1015376-how-would-you-do-a-cicada-3301-parody-in-werewolf?p=1015948#post1015948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bGood point. Also, the owner of this group views this all as a very complex game. Just picture Jigsaw, except with less death traps. Also, the death traps are really for &quot;cheaters&quot;. Also, the organization could be named after a chess piece, but which piece?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I like the Cicada<i> nom de guerre</i>, fits in kinda with the insect/arachnid theme of the Weaver. Maybe the individual members of the group could have names after chess pieces? That subtly reinforces the idea that it is a game. Mr. Bishop, Jacob Pawn, Ian Rook. That might be a bit on the nose, perhaps alluding to the fact that it is all a big chess game might be more fun for the players to figure out. If you want it to be really low-key, you could have the 'Queen' be named something like Isabella, Mary or Victoria, after a famous historical queen. Famous Pontifs for the Bishops, and famous knights and castles for the knights and rooks.<br /> <br /> Have you taken a gander at the book of the Weaver and Possessed? Both might help you model the crazed but calculating mindset of Grandmother Spider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 12-11-2016, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T20:10:09-08:00","id":1015953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1015376-how-would-you-do-a-cicada-3301-parody-in-werewolf?p=1015952#post1015952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, I like the Cicada<i> nom de guerre</i>, fits in kinda with the insect/arachnid theme of the Weaver. Maybe the individual members of the group could have names after chess pieces? That subtly reinforces the idea that it is a game. Mr. Bishop, Jacob Pawn, Ian Rook. That might be a bit on the nose, perhaps alluding to the fact that it is all a big chess game might be more fun for the players to figure out. If you want it to be really low-key, you could have the 'Queen' be named something like Isabella, Mary and Victoria, after a famous historical queen. Famous Pontifs for the Bishops, and famous knights and castles for the knights and rooks.<br /> <br /> Have you taken a gander at the book of the Weaver and Possessed? Both might help you model the crazed but calculating mindset of Grandmother Spider.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNot yet. For name, I could call them Scorpion. Also, I would think that the agents would be more passive then aggressive, not fighting garou, but observing them solve the puzzles. Also, I was thinking that one of the clues leads to a obstacle course,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T09:49:02-08:00","id":1016141,"title":"","content":"again, Weaver Drone Recruitment Center. or Shinzui Recruitment Center","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T10:07:06-08:00","id":1016145,"title":"","content":"I actually thought of them being sponsored by shinzui.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T13:54:15-08:00","id":1016721,"title":"","content":"I could write the group's backstory to give some more info. Also, they came into contact with Shinzui and the Weaver after a drone managed to complete their game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}